const language = [
{category:'People & connections · 人与关系',insight:'A friend can be a classmate, but not every classmate is already a friend. These words describe different relationships.',words:[
['friend','朋友','A person you know well and like.','a good friend','Mei is my friend.','Mei and I like spending time together. She is my ___.'],
['classmate','同班同学','Someone in the same class; this describes a school connection.','my classmate','Lin is my classmate.','Lin and I are in the same class. He is my ___.'],
['teacher','老师','Someone who helps people learn.','an English teacher','Our teacher is kind.','Ms Li helps us learn English. She is our ___.'],
['family','家人；家庭','A group of related people, not just one friend.','my family','My family is at home.','My parents and my brother are my ___.']],expressions:[
['Nice to meet you.','很高兴认识你。','Use when you meet someone for the first time.','Nice to ___ you.','meet'],
['This is my…','这是我的……','Use this to introduce a person or show an object.','This ___ my friend Mei.','is']],task:'Introduce one friend and one family member. Use “This is…” and choose am, is or are.'},
{category:'Daily habits · 日常习惯',insight:'Read, study, learn and practise describe related activities. Reading is one way to study; learning is what develops, and practice helps it last.',words:[
['read','阅读','Look at written language and understand it.','read a story','I read a story every morning.','I open a storybook and ___ it.'],
['study','学习；研究','Spend time working on a subject.','study English','We study English after school.','We work on English as a school subject. We ___ English.'],
['learn','学会；学习','Gain new knowledge or a skill.','learn a new word','I learn a new word each day.','With help, I gain a new skill. I ___ to swim.'],
['practise','练习','Do an activity again to improve; British verb spelling.','practise speaking','I practise speaking with Mei.','I repeat a skill to improve it. I ___ speaking.']],expressions:[
['every day','每天','Two words for frequency. “Everyday” is an adjective: everyday life.','I read every ___.','day'],
['get ready for','为……做好准备','Use for preparations before school or an activity.','I get ready ___ school at seven.','for']],task:'Describe your morning routine in three sentences. Include one activity and “every day”.'},
{category:'Actions in progress · 正在进行的动作',insight:'Look, watch and see all relate to vision. Look is a deliberate action, watch involves attention over time, and see can happen without trying.',words:[
['look','看；朝某处看','Direct your eyes deliberately. Use “look at” before an object.','look at a picture','I am looking at a picture.','I turn my eyes towards the picture. I ___ at it.'],
['watch','观看；注视','Pay attention to something happening over time.','watch a game','We are watching a game.','We follow the game as it happens. We ___ it.'],
['see','看见','Notice something with your eyes; often describes perception.','see a bird','I can see a bird outside.','Without trying, I notice a bird. I can ___ it.'],
['notice','注意到','Become aware of a detail or change.','notice a change','I notice a new leaf on the plant.','I become aware of a small change. I ___ it.']],expressions:[
['at the moment','此刻；目前','A useful time phrase for something happening now.','She is reading at the ___.','moment'],
['wait for','等待','The person or thing comes after “for”.','We are waiting ___ the rain to stop.','for']],task:'Look around you. Describe two actions happening now and one detail you can see.'},
{category:'Stories & discovery · 故事与发现',insight:'Find is a result; search is an effort. You can search carefully without finding anything. Discover often introduces something previously unknown.',words:[
['find','找到','Locate something; the past form is “found”.','find a notebook','Mei found my notebook beside the door.','After looking everywhere, I finally ___ my notebook.'],
['search','搜寻','Try to locate something; success is not guaranteed.','search for a key','We searched for the missing key.','We do not know where the key is. We ___ for it.'],
['discover','发现','Find out something previously unknown to you.','discover a new place','We discovered a quiet path behind the farm.','We learn about a place we never knew existed. We ___ it.'],
['explore','探索','Examine a place or idea to learn more about it.','explore a village','Our class explored the village.','We visit different parts of a village to learn about it. We ___ it.']],expressions:[
['for the first time','第一次','Put this after an action to describe a new experience.','I performed on stage for the first ___.','time'],
['learn from a mistake','从错误中学习','An error can lead to a better decision next time.','I learned ___ my mistake.','from']],task:'Write a four-sentence account of a visit. Include a past-tense verb and a discovery.'},
{category:'Comparing choices · 比较与选择',insight:'Cheap concerns price, useful concerns practical value, and convenient concerns ease. A cheaper choice is not always more useful or more convenient.',words:[
['cheap','便宜的','Low in price; sometimes suggests low quality, depending on context.','a cheap ticket','This ticket is cheaper than that one.','This ticket costs less money. It is ___.'],
['useful','有用的','Helps you do something or meet a need.','a useful tool','The lamp is useful for reading.','The tool helps me finish a task. It is ___.'],
['convenient','方便的','Fits your needs with little difficulty or wasted time.','a convenient location','The shop is in a convenient location.','The shop is easy to reach on my way home. Its location is ___.'],
['valuable','宝贵的；有价值的','Has worth, which may be practical, emotional or financial.','valuable advice','Her advice was more valuable than a gift.','Her advice was important and worth remembering. It was ___.']],expressions:[
['compared with','与……相比','Introduce the other item in a comparison.','Compared ___ the old route, this one is quieter.','with'],
['make a choice','作出选择','“Make” is the usual verb with “choice”.','We need to ___ a choice.','make']],task:'Compare two ways to school. Consider price, time and convenience, then justify your choice.'},
{category:'Effort & progress · 努力与进步',insight:'Improve means become better; achieve means reach an outcome. Encourage describes support, while persist describes continuing despite difficulty.',words:[
['improve','改善；提高','Become better, or make something better.','improve a skill','My reading has improved this term.','My skill has become better. It has begun to ___.'],
['achieve','实现；达成','Successfully reach a goal through effort.','achieve a goal','We have achieved our reading goal.','We work until we reach our goal. We ___ it.'],
['encourage','鼓励','Give someone confidence or support to act.','encourage someone to try','My coach has encouraged me to try again.','The coach gives me confidence to try. She wants to ___ me.'],
['persist','坚持','Continue despite difficulty; often followed by “in” + -ing.','persist in practising','She has persisted in practising every week.','She keeps going despite setbacks. She chooses to ___.']],expressions:[
['make progress','取得进步','Progress is normally uncountable: not “make a progress”.','I have made ___ in reading.','progress'],
['so far','到目前为止','Refers to the period up to now; often pairs with the present perfect.','We have read ten books so ___.','far']],task:'Describe something you have improved so far. Contrast a past difficulty with your current ability.'},
{category:'Harm, repair & risk · 损害、修复与风险',insight:'Damage usually means harm has occurred. Risk words can describe danger before harm happens. These distinctions help you read news accurately.',words:[
['damage','损坏；损害','Cause physical harm or reduce quality. Also an uncountable noun: “some damage”.','damage a bridge','The bridge was damaged by a storm.','A storm can physically harm a bridge. It can ___ it.'],
['harm','伤害；损害','A broad word for injury or negative effects on people, nature or interests.','harm wildlife','Pollution can harm wildlife.','Pollution has negative effects on animals. It can ___ wildlife.'],
['repair','修理；修复','Restore something broken or damaged to a usable condition.','repair a bridge','The bridge was repaired by local workers.','Workers restore a broken bridge. They ___ it.'],
['protect','保护','Keep someone or something safe from harm.','protect the environment','Young trees are protected from strong winds.','We keep young trees safe from the wind. We ___ them.']],expressions:[
['be made of','由……制成','Use when the material is still recognisable: a table made of wood.','The table is made ___ wood.','of'],
['be encouraged to','被鼓励去……','A useful passive pattern: be + encouraged + to + verb.','Students are encouraged ___ recycle paper.','to']],task:'Explain how a damaged object is repaired. Use the passive voice and distinguish prevention from repair.'},
{category:'Working with others · 合作与贡献',insight:'Help is broad. Support can be ongoing or emotional; assist often sounds more formal; contribute focuses on what someone adds to a shared outcome.',words:[
['help','帮助','A general, everyday word for making something easier.','help someone with a task','A neighbour helped us with the repair.','In everyday conversation, we ask someone to ___ us with a task.'],
['assist','协助','Help with a task; often more formal or specific.','assist with an experiment','Volunteers assisted with the experiment.','In a formal report, volunteers ___ with an experiment.'],
['support','支持','Provide encouragement, resources or continuing backing.','support a project','The engineer supported the students throughout the project.','A sponsor provides resources over time to ___ a project.'],
['contribute','贡献','Give effort, ideas or resources to something shared. Use “contribute to”.','contribute to a project','Each student contributed an idea to the project.','Each member adds ideas to a shared project. They ___ to it.']],expressions:[
['make a difference','产生影响；起作用','Describes a meaningful effect on a situation.','Small repairs can make a ___.','difference'],
['work together to','共同努力去……','Use “to” + verb to explain a shared purpose.','We work together ___ reduce waste.','to']],task:'Describe a person who contributed to a project. Use a relative clause and explain their contribution.'},
{category:'Evidence & certainty · 证据与确定性',insight:'A claim is something said to be true. Evidence can support it. An assumption is accepted without proof. An inference is a conclusion drawn from evidence; it may still be uncertain.',words:[
['claim','声称；主张','A statement presented as true, which may need checking.','make a claim','The report makes a claim about water use.','A statement is presented as true before it is checked. It is a ___.'],
['evidence','证据','Information that supports or challenges a conclusion; normally uncountable.','reliable evidence','We need reliable evidence before changing the timetable.','We need reliable information that supports a conclusion. We need ___.'],
['assumption','未经证实的假定','Something accepted as true without sufficient verification.','challenge an assumption','The survey challenged our initial assumption.','We accept an idea without checking it. We have made an ___.'],
['inference','推断','A conclusion reached by reasoning from available information.','draw an inference','Readers drew an inference from the data.','A reader reasons from evidence to a conclusion. This is an ___.']],expressions:[
['draw a conclusion','得出结论','Use a conclusion supported by evidence, not simply a guess.','We cannot ___ a conclusion from this figure alone.','draw'],
['take into account','把……考虑在内','Include a relevant factor when making a judgement.','We must take travel time into ___.','account']],task:'Identify one claim in an article. Explain what evidence would support it and what remains uncertain.'},
{category:'Degrees of harm & risk · 损害、削弱与危及',insight:'These words overlap but describe different mechanisms. Damage can describe harm already done. Undermine stresses weakening; compromise stresses impaired standards or integrity; jeopardize stresses exposure to danger. A risk need not become actual damage.',words:[
['damage','损害；破坏','Cause harm or loss of quality; common for physical objects, reputation and relationships.','damage a reputation','The false report damaged the organisation’s reputation.','A storm caused physical harm to the roof. The verb most directly describing that harm is ___.'],
['undermine','逐渐削弱；动摇','Weaken a foundation, authority, confidence or effectiveness; sometimes gradually or indirectly.','undermine confidence','Repeated contradictions undermined confidence in the report.','Repeated contradictions gradually weakened confidence. They began to ___ it.'],
['compromise','损害；使受影响；妥协','As a harm verb, weaken safety, integrity or standards. As a noun or another verb sense, it can mean a negotiated settlement.','compromise safety','Skipping inspections could compromise safety.','Use the common collocation for impaired safety: skipping checks could ___ safety.'],
['jeopardize','危及；使处于危险中','Put something valuable at risk; does not say that the bad outcome has already occurred. Also spelled “jeopardise”.','jeopardize a chance','An unsupported accusation could jeopardize the chance of cooperation.','No harm has happened yet, but an action puts success at risk. It could ___ the project.']],expressions:[
['put…at risk','使……面临风险','A plain alternative to “jeopardize”; risk does not mean harm is certain.','The decision could put the project at ___.','risk'],
['call into question','对……提出质疑','Raise doubts about validity; it does not by itself prove something false.','The missing context calls the conclusion into ___.','question']],task:'Compare “damaged the project” with “jeopardized the project”. Explain which implies actual harm and which describes risk. Write a conditional sentence for each.'}
];
